{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482133-balefire-for-autumn-and-winter-court","id":1482133,"title":"Balefire for Autumn and Winter Court?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-28T00:13:56-07:00","id":1482133,"title":"Balefire for Autumn and Winter Court?","content":"So, I've been reading Changeling and from what I understood every Freehold needs to have a Balefire, right? My doubt is purely esthetical, are Winter and Autumn Freeholds also centered around a fire or could it be something else that fits better their courts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T18:19:42-07:00","id":1482208,"title":"","content":"Personally I would interpret &quot;balefire&quot; very liberally. While always described as a fire, in terms of game mechanics it just needs to be the &quot;source&quot; of Glamour for the freehold.<br /> <br /> There already exists a variant of that - the &quot;sacred stone&quot; of Glades. I don't recall what the Merfolk use in their undersea freeholds, but most likely it isn't fire but something else.<br /> <br /> So I don't see a problem with using different flavor text to describe yet another alternative form. As long as it is something that could be stolen, extinguished, etc. and fits a fairy tale theme, it should work fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T18:35:09-07:00","id":1482211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482133-balefire-for-autumn-and-winter-court?p=1482208#post1482208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would interpret &quot;balefire&quot; very liberally. While always described as a fire, in terms of game mechanics it just needs to be the &quot;source&quot; of Glamour for the freehold.<br /> <br /> There already exists a variant of that - the &quot;sacred stone&quot; of Glades. I don't recall what the Merfolk use in their undersea freeholds, but most likely it isn't fire but something else.<br /> <br /> So I don't see a problem with using different flavor text to describe yet another alternative form. As long as it is something that could be stolen, extinguished, etc. and fits a fairy tale theme, it should work fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice, I was thinking about using magical crystals as the source of glamour in an ice cave winter Freehold. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T20:28:35-07:00","id":1482331,"title":"","content":"Strictly speaking it must be, indeed, a &quot;fire&quot;. Not because only fire can sustain such an arrangement, but because a Freehold isn't just a generic name for a Dreaming safe place, but a specific creation and tradition of the Kithain. Some Kiths may have alternatives to Freeholds, other Gallain do so, and there are natural places, too, like the Glades.<br /> <br /> That said, though, being more versatile isn't at all a problem. If your crystals can light up and are warm to the touch they're already &quot;fire&quot; enough for canon, and if not it won't make a huge deal of a difference. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said, as long as it can be stolen or extinguished/broken anything goes, although ideally it must also be able to kindle another fire, as this is how you usually creates new Freeholds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T21:03:53-07:00","id":1482336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482133-balefire-for-autumn-and-winter-court?p=1482331#post1482331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly speaking it must be, indeed, a &quot;fire&quot;. Not because only fire can sustain such an arrangement, but because a Freehold isn't just a generic name for a Dreaming safe place, but a specific creation and tradition of the Kithain. Some Kiths may have alternatives to Freeholds, other Gallain do so, and there are natural places, too, like the Glades.<br /> <br /> That said, though, being more versatile isn't at all a problem. If your crystals can light up and are warm to the touch they're already &quot;fire&quot; enough for canon, and if not it won't make a huge deal of a difference. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> said, as long as it can be stolen or extinguished/broken anything goes, although ideally it must also be able to kindle another fire, as this is how you usually creates new Freeholds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, I needed another opinion here. I'm still thinking about what could be the &quot;Balefire&quot; for this winter court Freehold. Still considering my options, so to speak. The &quot;magical crystals&quot; one was just in case I don't come up with anything really interesting, as always I'm open for ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T21:27:08-07:00","id":1482342,"title":"","content":"A magical lamp with bright red fire encased in purple-tinted glass, it hardens ice around it instead of melting it. Its main purpose is to serve as the &quot;ice forge&quot; of the Freehold, where artisans use the Balefire to repair tools and materials, but only the Freeholder enters the Cold Room, that despite the name is actually warm by the fire of the lamp and oversees the Ice Forge below, where no one can pass the night without express permission.<br /> <br /> Balefires may double as almost anything in the Freehold, and be of any size as fire as long as a piece of it can be somehow moved. Even when stealing or extinguishing it, intent and Glamour counts a lot, so you don't even need to constrain yourself with size. A Changeling that goes through all the steps to steal it can take any part of the Balefire and it will die out because for all purposes it was stolen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T21:46:04-07:00","id":1482344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1482133-balefire-for-autumn-and-winter-court?p=1482342#post1482342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A magical lamp with bright red fire encased in purple-tinted glass, it hardens ice around it instead of melting it. Its main purpose is to serve as the &quot;ice forge&quot; of the Freehold, where artisans use the Balefire to repair tools and materials, but only the Freeholder enters the Cold Room, that despite the name is actually warm by the fire of the lamp and oversees the Ice Forge below, where no one can pass the night without express permission.<br /> <br /> Balefires may double as almost anything in the Freehold, and be of any size as fire as long as a piece of it can be somehow moved. Even when stealing or extinguishing it, intent and Glamour counts a lot, so you don't even need to constrain yourself with size. A Changeling that goes through all the steps to steal it can take any part of the Balefire and it will die out because for all purposes it was stolen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That seems very interesting indeed. Thank you very much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}